From 3d2a514e369464fff60ff1cfe2aba5726e1e95f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shircomay <112399495+shircomay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:21:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(audio): add EchoCancellation package with vendored
 SpeexDSP

Meeting recordings average the microphone and the captured app audio. On
speakers the microphone also hears the remote voices, so they end up in the
mix twice. Removing that echo needs an acoustic echo canceller and a way to
line the two streams up in time.

This adds the building blocks as a local Swift package, with no app
integration yet:

- CSpeexDSP: the SpeexDSP echo canceller (MDF) and preprocessor vendored as
  a C target (BSD-3-Clause, files byte-identical to the pinned upstream
  commit, see VENDORED.md; attribution added to THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
- EchoCancellerBackend / SpeexEchoCanceller: a small backend protocol and
  the Speex implementation (float build, 10 ms frames, 300 ms filter,
  residual echo suppression).
- EchoCancellationStage: places the microphone and the reference on one
  sample timeline from host timestamps, holds a mic frame up to 150 ms for
  its reference, feeds the reference 30 ms ahead, treats reference gaps
  (ScreenCaptureKit stops delivering during silence) as silence, and never
  adds or drops a microphone sample.
- Tests (synthetic, seeded echo) for the backend, the timeline and the
  stage, TUNING.md with the measured numbers behind the defaults, and the
  small C/Python harness in Tools/linux-harness used to produce them.

The package is linked into the Mila and MilaTests targets in project.yml;
nothing imports it yet.

